{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-c3-history.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 86 gave the applied-state finding the same driven-history basis the recovery finding received.\\n\\nWhy. C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector was confirmed with a limitation on record: the committed records were prepared or driven as in the C1 checks, so the history that produced them was not constructed. The driven-history harness now produces them through the implementation itself — the owner admits a client proposal, runs a real PreAccept round, fast-commits and broadcasts the Commit to another replica, which installs it — and then a replica that never saw the instance recovers it, with the recoverer committing a NOOP vector while the other two hold the real command. Each replica's committed record is then applied through the real executor and the effects for the instance's key are compared.\\n\\nWhat was submitted. A new artifact on the same unit (unit-C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector) with the reviewed plan and the driven-history harness: the prerequisite reply that the recovery ignores comes from the committing replica's own handlers, the applied-state event reports each replica's effect, and the property asserts applied_match == true — which the local construction run reports false, with the recoverer's state machine holding no value while the other two hold the real PUT. The obligation, predicate, prerequisites, identity correlation and binding are unchanged; only the input history is upgraded, so the claim's prepared-record caveat is removed while its remaining limits (direct execution rather than the production loop, one instance and one key, the N=3 Thrifty configuration) stay declared.\\n\\nFrontier. Twelve claim families are settled, and this artifact awaits the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review; the map is current at version 17, the two candidates remain paused with scoped resume conditions, the single in-exercisable item is still the reader-side reaction to a displaced stream, and the attribution issue on the superseded C1 artifact remains visible as bookkeeping only. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
